// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// The angled form, which must NOT look beside the including file.
//
// `#include <common.idl>` resolves only along the search path, so this file is
// accepted with `-I corpus/include` and rejected without it — even though
// `common.idl` is its next-door neighbour.  That asymmetry is the C convention
// CORBA IDL inherits, and getting it wrong makes an estate resolve differently
// depending on which directory the validator was invoked from.
//
// 꺾쇠 형식은 인클루드하는 파일 옆을 보지 않는다.  `-I` 없이는 거부된다.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

#include <common.idl>

module Angled {
    typedef ::Freight::StampText Label;
};
